# Serene Ultra — English (US) shader menu labels

screen.QUALITY = Quality & Profiles
screen.COLOR = Color & HDR Controls

option.SHADOW_ALPHA_CUTOFF = Shadow Alpha Cutoff
option.AO_STRENGTH = Contact AO Strength
option.AO_RADIUS = Contact AO Radius
option.RED_GAIN = Red Channel
option.GREEN_GAIN = Green Channel
option.BLUE_GAIN = Blue Channel
option.GAMMA = Gamma
option.EXPOSURE = Exposure
option.CONTRAST = Contrast
option.SATURATION = Saturation
option.HDR_LOOK = HDR Tone Mapping

option.SHADOW_ALPHA_CUTOFF.comment = Controls which transparent texels are removed from shadow casters. Lower values preserve finer foliage detail.
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment = Controls local screen-space contact shading. AO affects ambient light only.
option.AO_RADIUS.comment = Sets the view-space radius used to detect nearby occluding surfaces. Larger values affect broader contact regions.
option.RED_GAIN.comment = Adjust the red channel independently. 1.00 is neutral.
option.GREEN_GAIN.comment = Adjust the green channel independently. 1.00 is neutral.
option.BLUE_GAIN.comment = Adjust the blue channel independently. 1.00 is neutral.
option.GAMMA.comment = Display gamma correction. 1.00 is neutral.
option.EXPOSURE.comment = Brightness adjustment in photographic stops.
option.CONTRAST.comment = Adjust contrast around middle gray.
option.SATURATION.comment = Adjust color intensity. 1.00 is neutral; 0.00 is monochrome.
option.HDR_LOOK.comment = HDR-style tone mapping for SDR output. This does not enable operating-system or monitor HDR output.

value.HDR_LOOK.0 = Neutral
value.HDR_LOOK.1 = HDR
value.HDR_LOOK.2 = Ultra HDR

profile.comment = Ultra-Light: lower shadow cost while retaining effects. Smooth: balanced shadow quality. Ultra: full shadow-distance target. HDR: Ultra with HDR-style tone mapping. Ultra-HDR: stronger highlight compression and HDR-style presentation. All profiles retain the complete planned feature set.

option.WATER_FOG_MULT = Water depth opacity
option.WATER_FOG_MULT.comment = Controls how quickly water becomes opaque with depth.

option.WEATHER_TEX_OPACITY = Weather particle opacity
option.WEATHER_TEX_OPACITY.comment = Adjusts the opacity of vanilla rain and snow textures.

option.WAVING_RAIN = Waving rain and snow
option.WAVING_RAIN.comment = Adds subtle wind-driven motion to falling rain and snow.

option.PARTICLE_MATERIAL_FEATURES = Particle material effects
option.PARTICLE_MATERIAL_FEATURES.comment = Detects water, rain, snow, smoke and emissive particle textures.

option.WATER_REFLECTION_QUALITY = Water / Glass Reflection Quality
option.WATER_REFLECTION_QUALITY.comment = Controls screen-space reflection steps for water and glass. Higher values improve hit coverage at additional GPU cost.

option.WATER_REFRACTION_STRENGTH = Water Refraction
option.WATER_REFRACTION_STRENGTH.comment = Controls half-resolution screen-space refraction through water. Set to 0 to disable distortion.
option.WATER_REFLECTION_STRENGTH = Water Fresnel Reflection
option.WATER_REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the strength of valid screen-space water reflections at grazing angles.

option.WATER_WAVE_STRENGTH = Water Wave Strength
option.WATER_WAVE_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the strength of three animated water-normal scales. Set to 0 to disable surface waves.
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED = Water Wave Speed
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED.comment = Controls relative animation speed. The selected wave octaves use integer texture periods so animation stays continuous when Iris frameTimeCounter wraps.

option.WATER_COLOR_STRENGTH = Water Style Tint
option.WATER_COLOR_STRENGTH.comment = Blends the Unbound-style water base tint with the sampled water atlas colour. Set to 0 to preserve the atlas colour.
option.WATER_NOISE_COLOR_STRENGTH = Water Colour Variation
option.WATER_NOISE_COLOR_STRENGTH.comment = Adds subtle animated colour variation using Iris noisetex. Set to 0 to disable the noise lookup.

option.WATER_FOAM_STRENGTH = Water Foam
option.WATER_FOAM_STRENGTH.comment = Controls foam at water and opaque-surface intersections. The effect is restricted to top-facing water surfaces.

option.WATER_UNDERWATER_STRENGTH = Underwater Water Response
option.WATER_UNDERWATER_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the cool tint, reduced opacity and softened reflections when the camera is underwater.

option.GLASS_REFLECTION_STRENGTH = Glass / Ice Reflections
option.GLASS_REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment = Controls screen-space reflections on clear, stained and tinted glass, plus translucent ice. Reflection quality follows the Water / Glass Reflection Quality setting.
option.PORTAL_EMISSION_STRENGTH = Nether Portal Emission
option.PORTAL_EMISSION_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the self-emission of nether portal surfaces.

option.MATERIAL_SPECULAR_STRENGTH = Material Specular Strength
option.MATERIAL_SPECULAR_STRENGTH.comment = Controls deferred highlights for oldPBR/LabPBR terrain materials and classified smooth blocks such as slime and honey.

option.MATERIAL_AO_STRENGTH = Material AO Lighting Strength
option.MATERIAL_AO_STRENGTH.comment = Controls how strongly stored material AO attenuates indirect/block lighting; direct celestial illumination remains unchanged.

option.MATERIAL_SSS_STRENGTH = Subsurface Scattering Strength
option.MATERIAL_SSS_STRENGTH.comment = Adds a low-cost backlighting approximation from LabPBR's subsurface channel. Porosity values are handled separately by wet-surface response.

option.WATER_ABSORPTION_STRENGTH = Water Absorption
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_STRENGTH.comment = Controls depth-dependent Beer-Lambert colour absorption in refracted water. Higher values attenuate red and green light more strongly, producing deeper blue water.

option.PORTAL_DISTORTION_STRENGTH = Nether Portal Distortion
option.PORTAL_DISTORTION_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the four-tap animated portal texture distortion. Samples are clamped to the current atlas sprite to prevent texture bleeding.

option.WATER_WAVE_SCALE = Water Wave Scale
option.WATER_WAVE_SCALE.comment = Controls the spatial frequency of the three animated wave bands. Higher values create shorter, more frequent waves.

option.WATER_CAUSTICS_STRENGTH = Water Caustics Strength
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the contrast of projected water caustics on terrain receiving sunlight.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_SCALE = Water Caustics Scale
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_SCALE.comment = Controls the spatial frequency of the projected water-light pattern.

option.WATER_NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH = Water Normal Map Strength
option.WATER_NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH.comment = Blends resource-pack PBR water normals into the animated surface normal. Neutral when no water normal map is supplied.

option.GLASS_NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH = Glass / Ice Normal Map Strength
option.GLASS_NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH.comment = Applies resource-pack PBR normal maps to glass and ice reflections. Neutral when no normal map is supplied.

option.OPAQUE_NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH = Opaque Normal Map Strength
option.OPAQUE_NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH.comment = Applies resource-pack PBR normal maps to terrain, entities and block entities. Neutral when no normal map is supplied.
option.PBR_AO_STRENGTH = LabPBR AO Map Influence
option.PBR_AO_STRENGTH.comment = Controls how strongly the LabPBR normal-map blue channel influences the material AO value. Zero ignores the map; 100 uses it fully.

option.PBR_REFLECTION_STRENGTH = PBR Reflection Strength
option.PBR_REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment = Fresnel-weighted screen-space and sky/horizon reflections on glossy opaque materials.
option.PBR_REFLECTION_QUALITY = PBR Reflection Quality
option.PBR_REFLECTION_QUALITY.comment = Screen-space reflection ray steps. Zero keeps the low-cost environment fallback.

option.RAIN_PUDDLE_STRENGTH = Rain Puddle Strength
option.RAIN_PUDDLE_STRENGTH.comment = Controls lightweight rain puddles on sky-exposed upward-facing terrain. LabPBR porosity reduces pooling, while leaves and farmland are excluded. Uses no 3D voxel map or extra render target.

option.MATERIAL_WETNESS_STRENGTH = Material Wetness Strength
option.MATERIAL_WETNESS_STRENGTH.comment = Controls porosity-driven darkening and reflectance loss on LabPBR materials when rain leaves surfaces wet.

option.POM_STRENGTH = Parallax / POM Strength
option.POM_STRENGTH.comment = Uses the resource pack's LabPBR or oldPBR normal-map alpha height channel for bounded terrain depth. Set to 0 to disable.
option.POM_QUALITY = Parallax Sample Quality
option.POM_QUALITY.comment = Number of bounded height samples per pixel. Higher values improve depth intersection but increase terrain shader cost.
option.POM_DISTANCE = Parallax Fade Distance
option.POM_DISTANCE.comment = POM fades smoothly to zero by this view distance. Shorter distances reduce GPU cost.

option.GENERATED_NORMAL_STRENGTH = Generated Normal Strength
option.GENERATED_NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment = Creates subtle tangent-space detail from albedo contrast when no resource-pack normal detail is present. Uses four bounded atlas samples; set to 0 for the lowest GPU cost.

option.COATED_TEXTURE_STRENGTH = Coated Texture Strength
option.COATED_TEXTURE_STRENGTH.comment = Adds subtle stable noise variation to dark opaque materials. Uses one noise lookup and fades with distance/mip level; set to 0 for the lowest GPU cost.

option.POM_ENTITY_STRENGTH = Entity Parallax / POM Strength
option.POM_ENTITY_STRENGTH.comment = Enables bounded LabPBR/oldPBR height mapping on opaque entity models. Item frames are excluded. Disabled in Ultra-Light and Smooth to protect low-end GPUs.

option.ENTITY_GN_AND_CT = Entity Generated Normals + Coating
option.ENTITY_GN_AND_CT.comment = Enables albedo-derived normal detail and stable noise coating on opaque entity models. Disabled by default to avoid extra texture reads on low-end GPUs; terrain and block-entity settings remain independent.

option.WATER_WAVE_DETAIL = Very Large Water Wave Detail
option.WATER_WAVE_DETAIL.comment = Adds Unbound-style very-large-scale normal detail with one extra texture sample. Disabled in Ultra-Light and Smooth to protect low-end GPUs.

option.HAND_PBR_STRENGTH = Held Item PBR Strength
option.HAND_PBR_STRENGTH.comment = Enables tangent-space normal maps, material reflectance and item-specific highlights on first-person held items. Set to 0 to skip the two extra PBR texture reads; Ultra-Light disables this path.

option.HELD_LIGHTING_STRENGTH = Held Item World Lighting
option.HELD_LIGHTING_STRENGTH.comment = Adds low-cost colored light from luminous main/offhand items to nearby opaque surfaces. Ultra-Light compiles it out; it adds no texture samples and does not cast shadows.

option.BLOOM_STRENGTH = Bloom Strength
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment = Combines a blurred half-resolution level with a wide quarter-resolution level for a soft multi-scale glow. It costs four small extra passes; Ultra-Light disables the chain entirely.
option.BLOOM_THRESHOLD = Bloom Highlight Threshold
option.BLOOM_THRESHOLD.comment = Sets the brightness where the bloom bright pass begins. Lower values make more surfaces glow; higher values restrict the effect to bright emissive and highlight pixels. The cutoff uses a soft knee so bloom ramps in instead of popping.

option.FXAA_ENABLED = Fast Approximate Anti-Aliasing
option.FXAA_ENABLED.comment = Applies edge-adaptive spatial anti-aliasing in the final pass without temporal history or an extra render target. Disable it for the lowest GPU cost.

option.LIGHT_SHAFT_STRENGTH = Sunlight Shafts
option.LIGHT_SHAFT_STRENGTH.comment = Adds a screen-space radial scattering approximation from bright visible sky toward opaque surfaces. It is strongest in clear daylight and uses no extra render target.
option.LIGHT_SHAFT_QUALITY = Light Shaft Quality
option.LIGHT_SHAFT_QUALITY.comment = Number of radial sky samples. Higher settings increase composite-pass texture reads; zero disables the effect.

option.SCREEN_GI_STRENGTH = Screen-Space Indirect Light
option.SCREEN_GI_STRENGTH.comment = Adds subtle depth-aware colour bounce from nearby visible surfaces. This is a low-cost screen-space approximation, not full world-space global illumination; it uses four neighbouring scene/depth samples.
